WEBVTT

00:00:00.008 --> 00:00:04.697
When you review the readmission project, keep three questions visible.

00:00:04.697 --> 00:00:08.902
First, what does one row represent at this stage?

00:00:08.902 --> 00:00:12.448
Second, what defines the sequence of events?

00:00:13.073 --> 00:00:19.730
Third, which operations preserve the admission rows, and which operations would collapse them?

00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:26.175
If you can answer those three questions, the query becomes much easier to explain and audit.

00:00:26.175 --> 00:00:31.615
Advanced S Q L should make reasoning more powerful, not less transparent.
